DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("ln((sqrt((5-x))))");
$fun_1 = Formula("(x^2-4*x+2)*5");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("({-5, -4, -2, 10} - {-5, -4, -2, 10})");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("([2, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ([2, infinity)))) U [2, infinity) U [2, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-5, -4, -2, 10}) U [2, infinity)");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("{-8, -5, 2, 4} U {-8, -5, 2, 4} U {0, 5, 10}");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("({0, 5, 10} - {0, 5, 10})");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

Lily collected [`15`] seashells on Monday. On Tuesday, she found [`2`] more seashells. On Wednesday, she discovered [`17`] additional seashells. However, on Thursday, she gave [`19`] seashells to her friend for an art project. How many seashells does Lily have left?

[_____]{15}
[%
15+2+17-19

First, calculate the seashells after Monday and Tuesday: 15 + 2 = 17 seashells. Then, add Wednesday's collection: 17 + 17 = 34 seashells. Finally, subtract the seashells given away on Thursday: 34 - 19 = 15 seashells.
%]
---

A pizza was cut into [`11`] equal slices. Xiao Mei ate [`5`] slices. Meanwhile, her brother received [`8`] empty boxes of crayons from his friend. How much of the pizza did Xiao Mei eat?

[_____]{0.454545454545}
[%
5/11+0*8

First, calculate the fraction of pizza Xiao Mei ate: 5 ÷ 11 ≈ 0.454545454545. Then, calculate the crayons from empty boxes: 0 × 8 = 0 (since empty boxes contain no crayons). Finally, add the results: 0.454545454545 + 0 = 0.454545454545 of the pizza.
%]
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-8, -5, 2, 4\}`]
- [`B = \{0, 5, 10\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup A \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`B - B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x \geq 2\}`]
- [`B = \{-5, -4, -2, 10\}`]

Compute:
- [`B - B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`(A \cap (A)) \cup A \cup A \cap B \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 4, 0, -1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 9, -8, -8 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<9, -8, -8>") x Compute("<4, 0, -1>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<9, -8, -8>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<9, -8, -8>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<9, -8, -8>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<9, -8, -8>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -7, 8, -4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 9, 1, 7 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-7, 8, -4>") x Compute("<9, 1, 7>")}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<9, 1, 7>") . Compute("<-7, 8, -4>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-7, 8, -4>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-7, 8, -4>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-7, 8, -4>") . Compute("<9, 1, 7>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(9) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>9)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(4) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>4)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
